The `TestExitCode` failure in that [last build ](https://teamcity.cockroachdb.com/viewLog.html?buildId=8419310&buildTypeId=Cockroach_BazelEssentialCi) is a real headscratcher. My read of the stack traces suggests that `runExitCodeTest(t, nil /* test passes */))` never returned and the test timed out after 55 seconds waiting on this select statement:
```
	if shutdownSleep := prometheusScrapeInterval - timeutil.Since(shutdownStart); shutdownSleep > 0 {
		ticker := time.NewTicker(shutdownSleep)
		select {
		case <-r.stopper.ShouldQuiesce():
		case <-ticker.C:
		}
	}
```
That implies that either the `shutdownSleep` had a value larger than 55s, which I think is impossible, or the ticker never sent any ticks which seems strange too. The `NewTicker` docstring does have this mysterious line: "The ticker will adjust
// the time interval or drop ticks to make up for slow receivers."

Even weirder, when I ran the test once on my gce worker, it failed immediately, but then when I tried to add a log line to print the `shutdownSleep` duration, I could not repro the failure under stress. Then, I tried stressing the original commit, and still no failure.

I added an additional commit to use `time.After` instead of a ticker, which makes more sense for this use case anyway. Hopefully no mysterious flakes in this build run.
